# Firmware that has a prebuilt equivalent in ::gentoo is taken prebuilt.
#
# sys-firmware/seabios: app-emulation/qemu depends on
#     || ( >=sys-firmware/seabios-X[seavgabios] >=sys-firmware/seabios-bin-X )
# and Portage takes the FIRST satisfiable alternative, so it compiled SeaBIOS.
# That build is PYTHON_COMPAT=( python3_{10..13} ): it brought dev-lang/python:3.13
# into the kde image, outside PYTHON_TARGETS=python3_14 (D15). Measured on the kde
# plan (2026-09-27): with this mask python:3.13 is gone and seabios-bin-1.16.3 is
# used; sys-power/iasl stays, because app-emulation/virtualbox builds with it too.
# The ebuild itself says "Please try sys-firmware/seabios-bin before requesting
# support". Masking the source package
# makes the || fall through to seabios-bin (no Python, no compiler), and a fork of
# the ebuild with python3_14 is not needed.
sys-firmware/seabios
